//
// GEMMA4-E2B Q4NX prefill correctness gate: run the prompt through the NPU
// prefill and score the result against the CPU reference this example already
// ships (gemma4_e2b_q4nx_weights.forward_prompt, itself gated per layer against
// FastFlowLM's golden activations by `make check`).
//
// THE ARGMAX ALONE IS NOT THE GATE, and that is the lesson this model taught
// twice: a doubled embedding scale and a per-layer-embedding input read from the
// wrong tensor BOTH still predicted ' Paris' here while the model was
// numerically broken. So the gate is the cosine of the whole 262144-wide logit
// vector against the reference, with the argmax match as a second, weaker
// condition -- run_reference.py says the same thing about its own smoke test.
//
// The companion to run_npu2_verify.lit: that one scores the DECODE path per
// layer, this one scores the PREFILL path end to end. Neither subsumes the
// other -- they are different engines over the same weights.
//
// Weights are the FastFlowLM model.q4nx bundle; no HF bf16 reference and so no
// hf_token, since that repo is ungated.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, peano_ge22, hfweights_fastflowlm_gemma4_e2b_it_npu2
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_npu2_verify_prefill
// RUN: cd test_npu2_verify_prefill
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile clean
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile compile-prefill PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile prefill-paris PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
//
// CHECK: *** PARIS ***
// A parsed cosine, not just the verdict line: if the reference comparison ever
// stopped running, GATE PASS would still print off the argmax alone and the
// real gate would have silently disappeared.
// CHECK: logit cosine vs CPU reference = 0.{{[0-9]+}}
// CHECK: GATE PASS
